<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orléans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cenabum, Aurelianum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orléans is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the Gallic town of Cenabum, whose massacre of Roman merchants in 52 BCE began the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>. Rebuilt by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> as Aurelianum, it became a Merovingian royal capital and a core town of the Capetian kings. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> relieved the English siege of the city in 1429.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orleans.jpg" alt="Orléans" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bmazerolles · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rue_Jeanne_dArc_Tramway_Orleans.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
